{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many Trinity homes have inadequate downspouts. Older properties may have original downspouts that are damaged or undersized. Extensions that once moved water away have been removed or kicked aside.</p>

<p>The result is water pooling near foundations. On Morgan County's clay soil, that water doesn't absorb — it spreads and persists. Over time, this leads to foundation cracks, basement moisture, and expensive repairs.</p>

<p>We're just 10 miles away in Hartselle and can quickly assess your property. We'll tell you exactly what you need — no more, no less.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>A good downspout system has three components: adequate capacity, proper positioning, and effective water dispersal.</p>

<p>Capacity means enough downspouts, sized for your roof and our rainfall. We often recommend 3x4 inch downspouts instead of standard 2x3 inch.</p>

<p>Positioning means placing downspouts where water naturally flows to corners and low points.</p>

<p>Water dispersal means getting water far from your foundation. Extensions move it a few feet. Underground drains can route it 10+ feet away.</p>
{% endset %}

